**Learner Use Cases**
Use Case 1: Register Account
Actor: Learner
Description:
The learner creates an account by entering their name, email address and password.
Main steps:
Learner opens the registration page.
Learner enters their details.
System validates the information.
System creates the learner account.
System directs the learner to the login page.
Expected result:
A learner account is created successfully.

Use case 2: Login
Actor: Learner / Facilitator
Description:
The user enters their email and password to access the system.
Main steps:
User enters email.
User enters password.
System checks the login details.
System identifies the user's role.
System displays the correct dashboard.
Expected result:
The user accesses the correct dashboard.

Use Case 3: View Dashboard
Actor: Learner
Description:
The learner views their learning information from one dashboard.
The dashboard displays:
Tasks
Completed tasks
Outstanding tasks
Progress
Assessments
Upcoming deadlines
Resources
Support sessions
Expected result:
The learner gets an overview of their current learning activities.

Use Case 4: Manage Tasks
Actor: Learner
Description:
The learner views assigned tasks and updates their task status.
Main steps:
Learner opens Tasks.
System displays available tasks.
Learner selects a task.
Learner completes the task.
Learner marks the task as completed.
System updates the task status.
Expected result:
The task changes from incomplete to completed.

Use Case 5: View Learning Resources
Actor: Learner
Description:
The learner accesses resources provided by the facilitator.
Main steps:
Learner opens Resources.
System displays available resources.
Learner selects a resource.
System opens the resource.
Expected result:
The learner accesses the selected study material.

Use Case 6: Complete Assessment
Actor: Learner
Description:
The learner completes and submits an assessment.
Main steps:
Learner opens Assessments.
Learner selects an assessment.
Learner completes the assessment.
Learner submits the assessment.
System records the submission.
Expected result:
The assessment is recorded as submitted.

Use Case 7: Book Support Session
Actor: Learner
Description:
The learner requests a support session with a facilitator.
Main steps:
Learner opens Support Sessions.
Learner selects a facilitator.
Learner selects a preferred date and time.
Learner enters the topic.
Learner adds notes if needed.
Learner submits the booking.
System records the booking as Pending.
Expected result:
The facilitator receives the support-session booking request.

**Facilitator Use Cases**
Use case 8: View Learner Progress
Actor: Facilitator
Description:
The facilitator views learner progress from the dashboard.
Main steps:
Facilitator logs in.
Facilitator opens the dashboard.
System displays learner progress.
Facilitator selects a learner.
System displays the learner's tasks, assessments and scores.
Expected result:
The facilitator gets an overview of the learner's progress.

Use Case 9: Create Task
Actor: Facilitator
Description:
The facilitator creates a task and assigns it to a learner.
Main steps:
Facilitator selects Add Task.
Facilitator enters the task title.
Facilitator selects a category.
Facilitator sets the due date.
Facilitator selects the priority.
Facilitator assigns the task.
System saves the task.
Expected result:
The task appears on the learner's dashboard.

Use Case 10: Upload Assessment
Actor: Facilitator
Description:
The facilitator adds an assessment for learners.
Main steps:
Facilitator selects Add Assessment.
Facilitator enters the assessment details.
Facilitator selects the assessment type.
Facilitator sets the due date.
Facilitator saves the assessment.
System makes the assessment available to learners.
Expected result:
Learners can access the assessment.

Use Case 11: Manage Support Bookings
Actor: Facilitator
Description:
The facilitator reviews and manages learner support-session requests.
Main steps:
Facilitator opens Support Sessions.
System displays pending bookings.
Facilitator selects a booking.
Facilitator confirms or rejects the request.
System updates the booking status.
Facilitator Can also book a sessionfor a learner that is struggling.
Expected result:
The learner sees the updated booking status.

Use Case 12: Manage Resources
Actor: Facilitator
Description:
The facilitator adds learning resources for learners.
Main steps:
Facilitator opens Resources.
Facilitator selects Add Resource.
Facilitator enters the title and description.
Facilitator selects the resource type.
Facilitator adds the resource link.
Facilitator saves the resource.
Expected result:
The resource becomes available to learners.